        "date": "2026-11-08T23:14:24Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): judge a modelled tool body by its revolved envelope\n\nA tool can carry a holder/assembly mesh (STEP, STL, OBJ through the model\nimporter), placed in the tool frame by a model axis direction and the\norigin's height above the tip, as one undoable command (SetToolBody:\nset / replace / clear). Its revolved envelope - per band along the axis,\nthe farthest the body reaches, every facet clipped exactly to each band -\nis what the stack laws judge:\n\n- the fixture laws (c2)/(d2), prismatic and posed, sweep the body's bands\n  in place of the holder cylinder (HolderStack; the cylinder stack keeps\n  the old sums, so a tool without a body is bit-identical);\n- every one-cylinder law (rest reach, solid law, multi-axis dodge, drill\n  reach, machine tool length) reads the cylinder enclosing the body,\n  which can only over-report.\n\nDegenerate, non-finite, flat, off-axis, below-tip, oversized and\ninto-the-flutes bodies refuse by name, at the command, at ChangeTool,\nat generation and on load. The body rides the op stamp only when present,\nsurvives DeleteTool/DeleteEntity undo, and saves as an optional `body`\non the tool row (project v54: an old reader must refuse rather than\njudge the smaller cylinder).\n\nFixes #368\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
