      "message": "feat(turning): judge a modelled lathe holder body against the revolved stock\n\nA turning insert, grooving/threading/form blade or boring bar may now\ncarry a holder body placed in the turning tool frame (tip = the point\nthe moves carry, +x radial away from the spindle in the path's meridian\nhalf plane, +z = lathe +Z), by nine numbers: the model's radial and\nspindle directions and its tip point (SetToolBody::lathe).\n\n- camcraft_tools::lathe_holder: the placement and the clearance bands\n  (per 0.25 mm band along the spindle, exact-clipped x and |y| spans),\n  whose radii bound every body point's distance from the axis for any\n  tip radius. Degenerate placements and meshes refuse by name.\n- operation::turning_holder: every move (feeds and rapids) walked at\n  0.25 mm; at each instant every band is read at its ends and at every\n  part/stock outline knot, facet vertex and grid station inside it,\n  against the part and the stock less the cuts before the instant (ops\n  and pilots ahead, the program ahead's facing, this path's earlier\n  cuts, this move's own footprint sweep - the excluded insert zone).\n  A rub is a new Warning::HolderHit { at, part, short_mm } that blocks\n  the post. A lathe body on a non-turning op refuses generation.\n- ToolBody carries its frame (BodyFrame::{Spindle, Lathe}); the file\n  writes a lathe body as `lathe` with no `axis`/`offset`, so an older\n  v54 reader refuses rather than misreads it.\n- A turning steel with no lathe body gets a non-blocking \"holder not\n  judged\" path note; no golden moved.\n\nDecisions: docs/decisions/369-lathe-holder-body.md\n\nFixes #369\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
